  "description": "NAMHAN crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H88 Dy6 N10 O32. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1D (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2D (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3D (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.525-3.996 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.77-114.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C78H88Dy6N10O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
